  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (+-)-Pantolactone may interact with Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular pathways involving Phosphodiesterase 6C. This interaction is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, all of which indicate that (+-)-Pantolactone targets Phosphodiesterase 6C, which in turn is a target of several related compounds. These compounds, including (1S,4R,8S,9R,10R,12R)-10-hydroxy-9-[(E,5S)-5-hydroxy-3-methyl-5-[(2S)-3-methyl-5-oxo-2H-furan-2-yl]pent-3-enyl]-4,8,10-trimethyl-2-oxatricyclo[6.3.1.04,12]dodecan-3-one and 2,5-dihydroxy-3-[(Z)-16-(2-hydroxy-5-methoxy-3,6-dioxocyclohexa-1,4-dien-1-yl)hexadec-8-enyl]-6-methylcyclohexa-2,5-diene-1,4-dione, are all linked to Neuropilin-2. The consistent presence of Phosphodiesterase 6C as a common target across these pathways suggests a potential mechanism by which (+-)-Pantolactone may influence Neuropilin-2 function. The evidence is robust and suggests a direct or indirect interaction, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
